.TH SENDTO 2
.SH NAME
sendto \- send one local datagram
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.PP
.B long sendto(int fd, const void *buf, unsigned long len, int flags, const struct sockaddr *addr, unsigned int addrlen);
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends one atomic AF_UNIX SOCK_DGRAM message to the bound pathname in addr.
Messages are bounded; a message larger than the native limit fails with EINVAL.
If the destination queue is full, the operation parks until space is available.
.SH ERRORS
EFAULT denotes malformed user buffers or addresses; ECONNREFUSED denotes an
unbound pathname; ENOTCONN denotes a datagram socket without a destination.
